"But 128 characters are not enough for the world. For years, different places made their own codes, and the same number could mean different characters on different computers. Text opened with the wrong code turned into nonsense. Unicode fixes this with one giant table for every writing system. The 2026 version, Unicode 18.0, lists 172,808 characters. The Chinese character 永 is number 27,704, usually written U+6C38. Most web pages store these numbers with a method called UTF-8, which uses one byte for an English letter and three bytes for a common Chinese character such as 永.": "ac7bb2b16520",
